  "reason": "The only completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) yielded ~48.5% accuracy, a very weak baseline that provides little guidance on which design axis matters most. The highest-uncertainty, highest-impact question is whether the image modality carries useful predictive signal at all. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest comparison to config_001: identical profile setting (singleprofile), same level of simplicity (no aggregation, no fusion), with only the modality swapped. If image-only substantially outperforms RNA-only, multimodal fusion (configs 16-51) becomes the primary direction; if it performs similarly poorly, I should focus on better single-modal representations (e.g., scgpt, scvi) rather than adding complexity. With 8 experiments remaining, establishing the per-modality ceiling before investing in fusion or encoder comparisons is the most information-efficient next step."
}

